Camille, Warrick,<br />
<br />
We are not answering that letter with an argument about migration gaps. We =
are answering it with a search.<br />
<br />
The Commission's electronic mail journal archive holds every message sent o=
r received on the messaging system, with attachments, going back to 2004, a=
nd its retention clock has been frozen by the destruction moratorium since =
2011. It is not indexed by examination number, which is why nobody reaches =
for it, but it is full-text searchable by mailbox and date through the eDis=
covery interface. If the staff obtained a written undertaking from Ottoway =
Trask in 2012, the undertaking was emailed to somebody, and the archive has=
 it.<br />
<br />
I want the search run on Count II specifically, and I want the result docum=
ented whichever way it comes out. If it produces the undertaking, Count II =
is proved out of the respondent's own file. If it produces nothing, that is=
 not an absence of evidence - that is a search of the one system that could=
 not have lost the document, and we will need to act on the answer.<br />
<br />
Han-Wei, please scope it.<br />
<br />
Gretchen Sallenave